IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`
IMPORT `chapter-16-sexual-general`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Sexual offences: penetration and related conduct`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 375, 376, 376A, 376AA, 376B, 376C, 376D, 376E, 376EA, 376EB,
-- 376EC, 376ED, 376EE, 376F, 376G, 376H, 377, 377B.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Shape of the group. ss 375 and 376 are the non-consensual penetration offences,
-- differing in what does the penetrating: s 375 is penile, s 376 everything else and
-- the causing of another to penetrate. ss 376A and 376AA are the age offences, where
-- consent is expressly irrelevant. ss 376B to 376D are commercial sex with a minor,
-- including abroad. ss 376E to 376EE are grooming, sexual communication, and sexual
-- activity or images in a minor's presence -- each in a below-16 form and an
-- exploitative 16-to-18 form. ss 376F and 376H are procurement of a consent that the
-- section then treats as no consent. s 376G is incest. ss 377 and 377B stand apart:
-- a corpse and a living animal, neither of which can consent at all.
--
-- The below-16 / 16-to-18 pairs are the Act's own device and they matter to the
-- encoding, because s 377D makes a mistake as to age a defence to the second of each
-- pair and never to the first. `a mistake as to age is a defence` therefore appears
-- as a negated conjunct on ss 376AA, 376EA, 376EC and 376EE, and on nothing else.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. Nearly every section here graduates its punishment by
-- the victim's age, by whether the relationship was exploitative, or by whether the
-- penetration was of a particular kind. Those facts are carried so a caller can see
-- them; no term is computed. s 375(3) and s 376(4) are encoded as their own
-- predicates because each states a distinct combination of conduct a caller may want
-- to test, not because a sentence follows from them.

§§ `The penetration limbs`

-- s 375(1) and (1A) are penile: penetrating the vagina of a woman, or the anus or
-- mouth of another person, with the penis.
-- s 376(2) covers the rest: sexual penetration with a part of the body other than
-- the penis or with anything else; causing a man to penetrate with his penis; and
-- causing another person to sexually penetrate.
-- ss 376A, 376AA and 376G each reuse all five limbs.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 375(1) and 375(1A)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is penile penetration` IF
        p's `a man penetrates with his penis the vagina of a woman`
    OR  p's `a man penetrates with his penis the anus or mouth of another person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376(2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is non-penile or caused penetration` IF
        p's `sexually penetrates with a part of the body other than the penis if a man or anything else the vagina or anus of another person`
    OR  p's `causes a man to penetrate with his penis the vagina anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
    OR  p's `causes another person to sexually penetrate with a part of that person body other than the penis if a man or anything else the vagina or anus of any person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 375 and 376"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is sexual penetration of any kind` IF
        `there is penile penetration` p
    OR  `there is non-penile or caused penetration` p

§§ `Section 375 -- Rape`

-- s 375(1) and (1A): penile penetration (a) without consent, or (b) with or without
-- consent where the other person is below 14.
--
-- s 375(5): despite s 79, no man is guilty under limb (a) if he proves that by
-- reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed the penetration was done with
-- consent. That is a defence to the non-consent limb only, so it is a negated
-- conjunct there and not on the below-14 limb.
-- s 375(4): no man is guilty under limb (b) for an act against his wife with her
-- consent. That is a carve-out on the below-14 limb only.
--
-- The two limbs are therefore not symmetrical, and are built separately before being
-- disjoined.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 375(1)(a) and (1A)(a), with s 375(5)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
      c IS A `Sexual Context`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 375 non-consent limb is made out` p c IF
        `there is penile penetration` p
    AND p's `the other person did not consent to the penetration`
    AND (NOT p's `the accused proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act of penetration was done with consent`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 375(1)(b) and (1A)(b), with s 375(4)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
      c IS A `Sexual Context`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 375 below-14 limb is made out` p c IF
        `there is penile penetration` p
    AND p's `the other person is below 14 years of age`
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 375"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes rape under Penal Code 1871 section 375
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Penile penetration of the vagina of a woman, or the anus or mouth of another person, without consent or where that person is below 14.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out for the below-14 limb.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes rape` p c IF
        `the section 375 non-consent limb is made out` p c
    OR  `the section 375 below-14 limb is made out` p c

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 375(3)"
@export Decide whether the rape is in the aggravated form of Penal Code 1871 section 375(3)
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Hurt caused or fear of death or hurt induced in order to commit or facilitate the offence, or an offence against a person below 14 without consent or in an exploitative relationship.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out, as for s 375 itself.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rape is in the section 375(3) aggravated form` p c IF
        `constitutes rape` p c
    AND (   p's `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of the offence voluntarily causes hurt to any person`
         OR p's `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of the offence puts a person in fear of death or hurt to that person or any other person`
         OR (    p's `the other person is below 14 years of age`
              AND p's `the other person did not consent to the penetration`)
         OR (    p's `the other person is below 14 years of age`
              AND p's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the other person`))

§§ `Section 376 -- Sexual assault involving penetration`

-- s 376(2): the three non-penile or caused limbs, where B did not consent or B is
-- below 14 whether or not B consented.
-- s 376(5): no offence (a) for an act against a spouse with that spouse's consent,
-- or (b) if despite s 79 the accused proves he believed in good faith by mistake of
-- fact that B consented AND that B was not below 14. Note limb (b) has two halves --
-- the belief in consent is not enough on its own where B was in fact below 14.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376(2), with s 376(5)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual assault involving penetration under Penal Code 1871 section 376
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Non-penile or caused penetration, without consent or against a person below 14.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out in s 376(5)(a).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual assault by penetration` p c IF
        `there is non-penile or caused penetration` p
    AND (   p's `the other person did not consent to the penetration`
         OR p's `the other person is below 14 years of age`)
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)
    AND (NOT (    p's `the accused proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act of penetration was done with consent`
              AND (NOT p's `the other person is below 14 years of age`)))

§§ `Sections 376A and 376AA -- Sexual penetration of a minor`

-- s 376A: any of the five penetration limbs against a person below 16. s 376A(1B)
-- puts the matter beyond doubt: the prosecution need not prove that B did consent,
-- and it is not a defence that B did. So consent plays no part in the rule at all.
-- s 376A(1A) is a displacement proviso -- the section does not apply to an act that
-- would be an offence under s 375 or s 376 -- so it is a negated conjunct.
-- s 376A(4): the spouse carve-out.
--
-- s 376AA: the same five limbs against a person of or above 16 but below 18, where
-- the accused is in a relationship exploitative of that person. s 376AA(2) again
-- makes consent irrelevant. This is a 16-to-18 offence, so s 377D(2) makes a
-- reasonable mistaken belief that the minor was 18 a defence -- unless one of the
-- s 377D(3) defeaters applies, which `a mistake as to age is a defence` decides.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual penetration of a minor below 16 under Penal Code 1871 section 376A
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Any of the five penetration limbs against a person below 16. Consent is irrelevant (s 376A(1B)).
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out in s 376A(4).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual penetration of a minor below 16` p c IF
        `there is sexual penetration of any kind` p
    AND p's `the other person is below 16 years of age`
    AND (NOT p's `the act would constitute an offence under section 375 or 376`)
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376AA"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exploitative sexual penetration of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 376AA
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Any of the five penetration limbs against a person of or above 16 but below 18, in a relationship exploitative of that person. Consent is irrelevant (s 376AA(2)).
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The exploitative-relationship test of s 377CA, and the s 377D mistake-as-to-age defence which is available on this section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exploitative sexual penetration of a minor` p c IF
        `there is sexual penetration of any kind` p
    AND p's `the other person is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
    AND `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` c
    AND (NOT `a mistake as to age is a defence` c)

§§ `Sections 376B, 376C and 376D -- Commercial sex with a minor below 18`

-- s 376B(1): obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18.
-- s 376B(2): communicating with another person for the purpose of so obtaining them.
-- s 376B(4) defines "sexual services" by reference to penetration or sexual
-- touching; that definition is carried inside the two facts rather than decided,
-- because it describes the service obtained and not the accused's own act.
-- s 376B(3): no offence for services obtained from the accused's spouse. Note this
-- carve-out has no consent requirement in its own words, but `the spouse carve-out
-- applies` is used for consistency across the group and is the stricter reading.
--
-- s 376C extends s 376B in three directions: a citizen or PR acting wholly outside
-- Singapore; a person acting in Singapore towards a minor outside it; and a person
-- acting outside Singapore towards a minor in it. Only the first is confined to
-- citizens and permanent residents.
-- s 376D punishes the facilitation of a s 376C offence -- travel arrangements,
-- transport, or publishing information to promote it -- and each limb is expressly
-- complete "whether or not such an offence is actually committed".

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes commercial sex with a minor below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 376B
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18, or communicating with another for the purpose of obtaining them.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out in s 376B(3).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes commercial sex with a minor` p c IF
        (   p's `obtains for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age`
         OR p's `communicates with another person for the purpose of obtaining for consideration the sexual services of a person below 18 years of age`)
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes commercial sex with a minor below 18 outside Singapore under Penal Code 1871 section 376C
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc A citizen or permanent resident acting outside Singapore, or anyone acting across the border in either direction, where the act would be a s 376B offence if done here.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes commercial sex with a minor outside Singapore` IF
        (    p's `the accused is a citizen or a permanent resident of Singapore`
         AND p's `does outside Singapore an act that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B`)
    OR  p's `does in Singapore an act involving a person below 18 years of age who is outside Singapore that would if that person were in Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B`
    OR  p's `does outside Singapore an act involving a person below 18 years of age who is in Singapore that would if done in Singapore constitute an offence under section 376B`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376D"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes organising a tour for commercial sex with a minor under Penal Code 1871 section 376D
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Making travel arrangements, transporting a person abroad, or publishing information, in each case to facilitate or promote a s 376C offence. The s 376C offence need not be committed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes organising a tour for commercial sex with a minor` IF
        p's `makes or organises travel arrangements for another person intending to facilitate the commission by that person of an offence under section 376C`
    OR  p's `transports another person to a place outside Singapore intending to facilitate the commission by that person of an offence under section 376C`
    OR  p's `prints publishes or distributes information intended to promote conduct that would constitute an offence under section 376C or to assist another to engage in such conduct`

§§ `Sections 376E and 376EA -- Sexual grooming`

-- Both sections require the accused to be 18 or above, to have met or communicated
-- with the minor on at least one previous occasion, one of the five meeting or
-- travelling acts in paragraph (a), and an intention at that time to do something to
-- or in respect of the minor that would involve a relevant offence.
--
-- The five acts in paragraph (a) are gathered into one fact. They are alternatives
-- of a single idea -- that a meeting was brought about -- and enumerating them would
-- add five booleans that no rule distinguishes between.
-- "Relevant offence" in s 376E(2) is a list of twenty sections plus provisions of two
-- other Acts. The Children and Young Persons Act 1993 and the Women's Charter 1961
-- are not in this source bundle, and most of the twenty are elsewhere in this
-- chapter, so the classification is a caller-asserted fact carried inside the
-- intention.
-- s 376E(3): it is immaterial whether the previous meeting or communication was in
-- or outside Singapore. That widens what may be asserted and adds no limb.
--
-- The two sections differ only in the age band and its belief test, and s 376EA adds
-- the exploitative relationship. s 376EA is a 16-to-18 offence, so the s 377D defence
-- applies to it and not to s 376E.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376E(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual grooming of a minor below 16 under Penal Code 1871 section 376E
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc An adult who, having met or communicated with a person below 16 before, brings about a meeting intending to commit a relevant offence, and does not reasonably believe that person to be 16 or above.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual grooming of a minor below 16` IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused had met or communicated with the other person on at least one previous occasion`
    AND p's `one of the five meeting or travelling acts in section 376E(1)(a) takes place`
    AND p's `at the time of that act the accused intends during or after the meeting to do anything to or in respect of the other person which would involve the commission by the accused of a relevant offence`
    AND p's `the other person is below 16 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 16 years of age`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376EA"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exploitative sexual grooming of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 376EA
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc As s 376E, but where the minor is of or above 16 but below 18 and the accused is in a relationship exploitative of that minor.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The exploitative-relationship test, and the s 377D mistake-as-to-age defence which is available on this section.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exploitative sexual grooming of a minor` p c IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused had met or communicated with the other person on at least one previous occasion`
    AND p's `one of the five meeting or travelling acts in section 376E(1)(a) takes place`
    AND p's `at the time of that act the accused intends during or after the meeting to do anything to or in respect of the other person which would involve the commission by the accused of a relevant offence`
    AND p's `the other person is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` c
    AND (NOT `a mistake as to age is a defence` c)

§§ `Sections 376EB and 376EC -- Sexual communication with a minor`

-- An adult who, for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing the
-- minor humiliation, alarm or distress, intentionally communicates with the minor,
-- where the communication is sexual and the minor is under the relevant age.
-- s 376EB(2) and s 376EC(2): it is immaterial whether the minor replied, and
-- immaterial where the communication originated provided either party was in
-- Singapore. The first adds no limb; the second is a jurisdictional condition and is
-- carried as the Singapore-presence fact.
-- s 376EB(4): the spouse carve-out, which s 376EC does not have.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376EB"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual communication with a minor below 16 under Penal Code 1871 section 376EB
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc An adult intentionally making a sexual communication to a person below 16 for sexual gratification or to cause humiliation, alarm or distress, with either party in Singapore.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc Whether the communication is sexual (s 377C(3)(d)), and the spouse carve-out in s 376EB(4).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual communication with a minor below 16` p c IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND p's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing the other person humiliation alarm or distress the accused intentionally communicated with that person`
    AND p's `the communication is sexual`
    AND p's `either the accused or the other person or both are in Singapore`
    AND p's `the other person is below 16 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 16 years of age`
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376EC"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exploitative sexual communication with a minor of or above 16 but below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 376EC
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc As s 376EB, but where the minor is of or above 16 but below 18 and the relationship is exploitative. There is no spouse carve-out in this section.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The exploitative-relationship test, and the s 377D mistake-as-to-age defence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exploitative sexual communication with a minor` p c IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND p's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing the other person humiliation alarm or distress the accused intentionally communicated with that person`
    AND p's `the communication is sexual`
    AND p's `either the accused or the other person or both are in Singapore`
    AND p's `the other person is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` c
    AND (NOT `a mistake as to age is a defence` c)

§§ `Sections 376ED and 376EE -- Sexual activity or image in a minor's presence`

-- Each section has two subsections: (1) engaging in a sexual activity in the minor's
-- presence, or where the minor can observe the accused, knowing or intending that
-- the minor be aware of it; and (2) intentionally causing the minor to observe a
-- sexual image. Both require the sexual-gratification-or-distress purpose, the age
-- band and its belief test, and a Singapore connection.
-- s 376ED(4): the spouse carve-out, which s 376EE does not have.
-- s 376EE adds the exploitative relationship and attracts the s 377D defence.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376ED(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sexual activity in presence limb is made out` IF
        p's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing the other person humiliation alarm or distress the accused intentionally engages in an activity`
    AND p's `the activity is sexual`
    AND p's `the accused engages in the activity when the other person is present or is in a place from which the accused can be observed`
    AND p's `the accused knows or believes that the other person is aware or intends that the other person should be aware that the accused is engaging in it`
    AND p's `either the accused or the other person or both are in Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376ED(2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sexual image limb is made out` IF
        p's `for the purpose of obtaining sexual gratification or of causing the other person humiliation alarm or distress the accused intentionally causes that person to observe an image`
    AND p's `the image is sexual`
    AND p's `either the accused or the other person or both are in Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376ED"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual activity or an image in the presence of a minor below 16 under Penal Code 1871 section 376ED
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc An adult engaging in a sexual activity in the minor's presence, or causing the minor to observe a sexual image, where the minor is below 16.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The spouse carve-out in s 376ED(4).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual activity or image before a minor below 16` p c IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND (   `the sexual activity in presence limb is made out` p
         OR `the sexual image limb is made out` p)
    AND p's `the other person is below 16 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 16 years of age`
    AND (NOT `the spouse carve-out applies` c)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376EE"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes exploitative sexual activity or an image in the presence of a minor of or above 16 but below 18 under Penal Code 1871 section 376EE
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc As s 376ED, but where the minor is of or above 16 but below 18 and the relationship is exploitative. There is no spouse carve-out in this section.
      c IS A `Sexual Context` @desc The exploitative-relationship test, and the s 377D mistake-as-to-age defence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes exploitative sexual activity or image before a minor` p c IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND (   `the sexual activity in presence limb is made out` p
         OR `the sexual image limb is made out` p)
    AND p's `the other person is of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`
    AND p's `the accused does not reasonably believe that the other person is of or above 18 years of age`
    AND `the relationship is exploitative of the minor` c
    AND (NOT `a mistake as to age is a defence` c)

§§ `Sections 376F and 376H -- Procurement of a sexual touching`

-- Both sections share a shape that is unusual in this chapter: the other person DOES
-- consent, and the offence lies in how the consent was procured.
--
-- s 376F: the touching is sexual and consented to, but the consent was obtained by
-- an inducement, threat or deception (or, where the other person is the accused's
-- spouse, by a threat or deception only -- an inducement offered to a spouse is not
-- enough), and that person has a mental disability the accused knows or could
-- reasonably be expected to know of. s 376F(5) defines mental disability as an
-- impairment that impairs the ability to make a proper judgment in giving consent to
-- sexual touching; that definition is carried inside the fact.
--
-- s 376H: the consent is obtained fraudulently by a deception or false
-- representation relating to a sexually protective measure or to the risk of a
-- sexually transmitted disease, known to the accused to have induced it. Note how
-- narrow the subject matter is -- s 376H(3)(c) defines "sexually protective measure"
-- and the deception must relate to that or to disease risk, not to anything else.
-- This is the same narrowing s 377CB performs for misconception generally.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376F"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes procurement of sexual activity with a person with mental disability under Penal Code 1871 section 376F
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc A consented sexual touching where the consent was procured by inducement, threat or deception (threat or deception only, if the other person is the accused's spouse), and that person has a mental disability the accused knows or ought to know of.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes procurement of sexual activity with a person with mental disability` IF
        p's `the accused intentionally touches another person or intentionally incites that person to touch the accused that person or another person`
    AND p's `the touching is sexual and the other person consents to the touching`
    AND (   p's `the accused obtains that consent by means of an inducement offered or given a threat made or a deception practised for that purpose`
         OR p's `the accused obtains that consent where the other person is the accused spouse by means of a threat made or a deception practised for that purpose`)
    AND p's `the other person has a mental disability`
    AND p's `the accused knows or could reasonably be expected to know that the other person has a mental disability`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376H"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes procurement of sexual activity by deception or false representation under Penal Code 1871 section 376H
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc A consented sexual touching where the consent was fraudulently obtained by a deception or false representation about a sexually protective measure or about the risk of a sexually transmitted disease, known to have induced it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes procurement of sexual activity by deception` IF
        p's `the accused intentionally touches another person or intentionally incites that person to touch the accused that person or another person`
    AND p's `the touching is sexual and the other person consents to the touching`
    AND p's `the accused fraudulently obtains the other person consent by means of a deception or false representation practised or made for that purpose`
    AND (   p's `the deception or false representation relates to the use or manner of use of any sexually protective measure`
         OR p's `the deception or false representation relates to the risk of the other person contracting a sexually transmitted disease from the touching`)
    AND p's `the accused knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of such deception or false representation`

§§ `Section 376G -- Incest`

-- Any person of or above 16 who penetrates, or causes or permits to be penetrated by,
-- a close family relative of or above 16, knowing that person to be a close family
-- relative.
-- s 376G(2) defines close family relative as grandchild, child, sibling, half-sibling,
-- parent or grandparent, whether or not the relationship is traced through lawful
-- wedlock. That definition is carried inside the relationship fact.
-- s 376G(4) is a displacement proviso: the section does not apply to an act that
-- would be an offence under s 375(1)(a), 375(1A)(a), 376(2) or 376AA(1).
-- s 376G(5): consent is neither to be proved nor a defence.
-- s 376G(6): a person below 18 who is the victim of a s 376AA offence is not guilty
-- under this section in respect of the same acts -- a carve-out for the exploited
-- minor, and a negated conjunct here.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 376G"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes incest under Penal Code 1871 section 376G
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Penetration of, or causing or permitting penetration by, a close family relative of or above 16, both parties being of or above 16, with knowledge of the relationship.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes incest` IF
        p's `the accused is of or above 16 years of age`
    AND p's `the other person is of or above 16 years of age and is a close family relative being a grandchild child sibling half-sibling parent or grandparent whether or not traced through lawful wedlock`
    AND (   `there is sexual penetration of any kind` p
         OR p's `causes or permits a close family relative to penetrate or sexually penetrate the accused`)
    AND p's `the accused knows that the other person is a close family relative`
    AND (NOT p's `the act would constitute an offence under section 375(1)(a) 375(1A)(a) 376(2) or 376AA(1)`)
    AND (NOT p's `the accused is a person below 18 years of age who is a victim of an offence under section 376AA in respect of the same acts`)

§§ `Sections 377 and 377B -- A corpse, and a living animal`

-- Neither section has a consent element as to the corpse or the animal, for the
-- obvious reason. What both do have is a second, far more serious limb where the
-- accused causes ANOTHER PERSON to do the act without that person's consent -- s 377(1)
-- (e) to (h) and s 377B(3). That non-consent is the element the encoding must keep,
-- and it is the only place consent appears in either section.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual penetration of a corpse under Penal Code 1871 section 377
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Penetration of or by a human corpse by the accused, or causing another person to do or undergo it without that person's consent.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual penetration of a corpse` IF
        p's `penetrates or sexually penetrates a human corpse or causes the accused own body to be so penetrated by a human corpse`
    OR  (    p's `causes another person to penetrate or sexually penetrate a human corpse or causes that person body to be so penetrated by a human corpse`
         AND p's `that other person did not consent to the penetration`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 377B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes sexual penetration with a living animal under Penal Code 1871 section 377B
GIVEN p IS A `Sexual Penetration` @desc Penetration of or by an animal by the accused, or causing another person to do or undergo it without that person's consent.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes sexual penetration with an animal` IF
        p's `penetrates with the accused penis the vagina anus or any orifice of an animal or causes or permits the accused vagina anus or mouth to be penetrated by the penis of an animal`
    OR  (    p's `causes a man to penetrate with his penis the vagina anus or any orifice of an animal or causes the vagina anus or mouth of another person to be penetrated with the penis of an animal`
         AND p's `that other person did not consent to the penetration`)

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes rape` IF
        `constitutes rape` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes sexual assault by penetration` IF
        `constitutes sexual assault by penetration` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes sexual penetration of a minor` IF
        (   `constitutes sexual penetration of a minor below 16` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes exploitative sexual penetration of a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes commercial sex with a minor` IF
        (   `constitutes commercial sex with a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes commercial sex with a minor outside Singapore` (a's `sexual penetration`)
         OR `constitutes organising a tour for commercial sex with a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes sexual grooming or communication with a minor` IF
        (   `constitutes sexual grooming of a minor below 16` (a's `sexual penetration`)
         OR `constitutes exploitative sexual grooming of a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes sexual communication with a minor below 16` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes exploitative sexual communication with a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes sexual activity or image before a minor below 16` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`)
         OR `constitutes exploitative sexual activity or image before a minor` (a's `sexual penetration`) (a's `sexual context`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes procurement of sexual activity` IF
        (   `constitutes procurement of sexual activity with a person with mental disability` (a's `sexual penetration`)
         OR `constitutes procurement of sexual activity by deception` (a's `sexual penetration`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes incest` IF
        `constitutes incest` (a's `sexual penetration`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
